    "label": {
      "en": "Limit complementary pension insurance, from 2014"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tscsepi_uplim"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This constant, expressed as an annual currency amount (38,340, tagged '#y' for a yearly value, and applicable from 2014 per the label), is the upper income limit of the band to which the complementary pension insurance contribution applies for self-employed industry-and-trade (I&T) workers. It is used as the Band_UpLim parameter of a SchedCalc in tscse_fr labelled 'I&T: Complementary pension insurance contributions for industry & trade', working together with the rate constant $tscsepi_industry_rate8 to cap the income range over which that band's rate is charged. The theme note indicates this complementary pension scheme's upper band extends up to 4 x PSS, consistent with this constant acting as that ceiling amount for the relevant historical year."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Parameters for self-employed contributions"
    },
